<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noviomagus Reginorum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Noviomagus Reginorum was the Roman town at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-sussex">West Sussex</a>, capital of the civitas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regni">Regni</a>. It grew up after the conquest of 43, probably under the client king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a>, and had a forum, baths, an amphitheatre and later stone walls. The street plan of modern Chichester still follows its main roads.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noviomagus-reginorum.jpg" alt="Noviomagus Reginorum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OLU · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chichester_Roman_Wall_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1012586.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
